## Query composer: core system direction
The composer is a foundational Relational Engine / Relational UI capability. Discover available node types, fields, operators and functions from the data/context and value types being queried. Candidate string functions include startsWith(), endsWith(), regex(); among() requires typed membership semantics. Names/syntax remain illustrative.

Engine owns typed query representation, operator/function definitions, compatibility, validation, composition and execution contracts. UI consumes that metadata for completion, hints and accessible keyboard/pointer editing; it must not maintain an unrelated hardcoded operator list. Agents should access the same discovery/validation contracts. Saved queries compose through query:. Exact grammar, evaluation constraints and pipeline semantics remain to design.

